{"parentUuid":"d472ec1d-3d6d-4fb7-8173-3cbe910ef6c5","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab26579806bc582bd","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01MqnMAxm9PY3DK39QhPXw1q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011QDHyF9ohpAM6TRXNFYWSy","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"anytime algorithm CP-SAT OR-Tools intermediate solution callback"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7744,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"output_tokens":339,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7744},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":339,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7744,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7744,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caox7V3EjYrSLchTaKRk7","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"86c275ba-11b7-45d4-a0df-fa38d4db2a9b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:14.820Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"cd2c47d7-81fe-4b8b-9f79-07e6221ee6fa","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"ab26579806bc582bd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UeFwNB1jcuXhfcgBtMiRyd","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"online bin packing 2024 2025 competitive ratio 1.58\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A new and improved algorithm for online bin packing | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/318260129_A_new_and_improved_algorithm_for_online_bin_packing\"},{\"title\":\"A new and improved algorithm for online bin packing\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1707.01728\"},{\"title\":\"The optimal absolute ratio for online bin packing\",\"url\":\"https://www.uni-siegen.de/fb6/aan/optimierung/publikationen/download/ft-jour-13.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Batched Bin Packing – Optimization Online\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/2004/02/826/\"},{\"title\":\"[2102.03311] Online Bin Packing with Predictions\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2102.03311\"},{\"title\":\"A New and Improved Algorithm for Online Bin Packing János Balogh\",\"url\":\"https://d-nb.info/1365945634/34\"},{\"title\":\"[1807.05554] A new lower bound for classic online bin packing\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1807.05554\"},{\"title\":\"Online Bin Packing with Predictions | Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research\",\"url\":\"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/view/14820\"},{\"title\":\"An asymptotic competitive scheme for online bin packing - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0304397515005150\"},{\"title\":\"A New and Improved Algorithm for Online Bin Packing - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.ESA.2018.5\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here are the key findings related to online bin packing and the 1.58 competitive ratio barrier:\n\n## Breakthrough Result Below 1.58\n\nAn algorithm called AH (Advanced Harmonic) achieved the first algorithm of asymptotic competitive ratio strictly below 1.58, with an asymptotic competitive ratio not exceeding 1.5783. This represents a significant milestone in online bin packing research, as it breaks through the long-standing 1.58 barrier that had existed previously.\n\n## Current Best Bounds\n\nAs of recent updates in 2024, the current best upper bound on the asymptotic competitive ratio is 1.7300245, while the current best lower bound on the asymptotic competitive ratio for k=3 is approximately 1.60555. This indicates ongoing research to tighten both upper and lower bounds on the competitive ratio.\n\n## Lower Bounds\n\nA lower bound on the asymptotic competitive ratio of any online algorithm for bin packing has been improved to above 1.54278. This establishes a gap between what is currently known to be achievable and what is theoretically possible for online bin packing algorithms.\n\nThe search results show active research in this area with continuous improvements being made to both algorithmic approaches and theoretical bounds.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"36d296fa-738b-4058-bc69-fba73bb80877","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:18.554Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cd2c47d7-81fe-4b8b-9f79-07e6221ee6fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"af7b32b8-19c0-44f0-be10-bf24e0611612","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"ab26579806bc582bd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XwpWyBZXXaQaYC8rLgjRBi","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"online combinatorial optimization survey 2025 competitive ratio placement\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"[2409.00075] A survey on combinatorial optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.00075\"},{\"title\":\"New Challenges in Combinatorial Optimization | Journal of Combinatorial Optimization | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10878-025-01330-2\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A survey on combinatorial optimization in dynamic environments\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/231969458_A_survey_on_combinatorial_optimization_in_dynamic_environments\"},{\"title\":\"A survey on combinatorial optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2409.00075v1\"},{\"title\":\"Approximation algorithms for combinatorial optimization with predictions | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=AEFVa6VMu1\"},{\"title\":\"Asymptotically Optimal Competitive Ratio for Online Allocation of Reusable Resources | Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/opre.2021.0695\"},{\"title\":\"Neural combinatorial optimization with reinforcement learning in industrial engineering: a survey | Artificial Intelligence Review | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10462-024-11045-1\"},{\"title\":\"neural combinatorial optimization\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=rJY3vK9eg\"},{\"title\":\"Accepted: 29 November 2024 / Published online: 14 February 2025\",\"url\":\"https://d-nb.info/1368674348/34\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) A survey on combinatorial optimization\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/383684287_A_survey_on_combinatorial_optimization\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding online combinatorial optimization, competitive ratios, and placement:\n\n## Recent Research Highlights\n\nPéter Györgyi, Tamás Kis, and Tímea Tamási consider the online variant of a combination of the joint replenishment problem with single machine scheduling, proposing a deterministic 2-competitive online algorithm for the general input.\n\nFor a certain class of inputs, the competitive ratio of the algorithm tends to √2 as the number of jobs tends to infinity.\n\n## Online Allocation Problems\n\nThe problem of online allocation (matching, budgeted allocations, and assortments) of reusable resources for which an adversarial sequence of resource requests is revealed over time has been studied, with recent work on asymptotically optimal competitive ratios for online allocation of reusable resources published in 2025.\n\n## Related Survey Work\n\nA comprehensive survey provides investigation of theories and recent advancements in applying reinforcement learning to solve hard combinatorial optimization problems, such as vehicle routing, bin packing, assignment, scheduling, and planning problems.\n\nThe search results indicate that online combinatorial optimization with competitive ratio analysis remains an active research area, particularly for scheduling and resource allocation problems with applications to practical scenarios like placement decisions.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"84fe8d04-f119-46ef-9e55-08399027d257","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:19.068Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"af7b32b8-19c0-44f0-be10-bf24e0611612","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"86c275ba-11b7-45d4-a0df-fa38d4db2a9b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"ab26579806bc582bd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011QDHyF9ohpAM6TRXNFYWSy","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"anytime algorithm CP-SAT OR-Tools intermediate solution callback\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Obtaining Intermediate Solutions in OR-Tools CP-SAT [Fixed]\",\"url\":\"https://www.technetexperts.com/ortools-intermediate-solutions-callback/\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"Setting solver limits | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_tasks\"},{\"title\":\"Find many CP-SAT solutions, multi-threaded, under time constraint\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/GNgvcMpEwmE\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Best way to generate multiple optimal/close-to-optimal solutions with CP-SAT\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/4DeoO5f7YXQ\"},{\"title\":\"CP_SAT Callback types\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/XuY3dozvVMI/m/35QBz1aNAQAJ\"},{\"title\":\"Google OR-Tools: ortools.sat.python.cp_model.CpSolverSolutionCallback Class Reference\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/python/classortools_1_1sat_1_1python_1_1cp__model_1_1CpSolverSolutionCallback.html\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"}]\n\nI found comprehensive information about anytime algorithms and intermediate solution callbacks in OR-Tools CP-SAT. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Anytime Algorithm Implementation with CP-SAT\n\nTo implement \"anytime\" algorithm behaviors where the system can provide the best-found-so-far solution if interrupted, senior architects must implement mechanisms to capture intermediate feasible solutions.\n\n## Solution Callback Mechanism\n\nThe CP-SAT solver provides a callback interface designed to monitor the search process. This class implements a callback that will be called at each new solution found during search, and the method on_solution_callback() will be called by the solver and must be implemented.\n\n## How Intermediate Solutions Work\n\nEvery time a solution is found, the solver ensures that any subsequent solution must strictly improve the objective value, and the default on_solution_callback method is only triggered when a better solution is discovered.\n\nIf the goal is to see \"intermediate\" results, those results are by definition the improving ones found during the search.\n\n## Implementation Options\n\nOR-Tools provides ObjectiveSolutionPrinter (to print objective values and elapsed time for intermediate solutions), VarArraySolutionPrinter (to print intermediate solutions with variable values and time), and VarArrayAndObjectiveSolutionPrinter (to print both intermediate solutions and objective values).\n\n## For Finding All Feasible Solutions\n\nIf the requirement is to find all feasible solutions regardless of the objective, the objective function must be removed or disabled, and the search parameter enumerate_all_solutions should be set to true.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"093c84de-6977-4a97-969d-ed9bc31eca62","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:22.503Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"86c275ba-11b7-45d4-a0df-fa38d4db2a9b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d472ec1d-3d6d-4fb7-8173-3cbe910ef6c5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"ab26579806bc582bd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01No5Fv5eRF7CXFFumnr7u7N","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"incremental SAT solving IPASIR-UP incremental constraint propagation 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research 81 (2024) 989-1017\",\"url\":\"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/download/16163/27111/42883\"},{\"title\":\"Certifying Incremental SAT Solving\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/FazekasPollittFleuryBiere-LPAR24.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"IGMaxHS – An Incremental MaxSAT Solver with Support for XOR Clauses\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2410.15897v1\"},{\"title\":\"Certifying Incremental SAT Solving Katalin Fazekas 1, Florian Pollitt\",\"url\":\"https://kfazekas.github.io/papers/FazekasPollittFleuryBiere-LPAR24.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Deep Integration of SAT Solving and Model Checking\",\"url\":\"https://froleyks.de/assets/pdf/Deep%20integration%20of%20SAT%20solving%20and%20model%20checking.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SHA-256 Collision Attack with Programmatic SAT\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2406.20072v1\"},{\"title\":\"Incremental Maximum Satisfiability - DROPS - Schloss Dagstuhl\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SAT.2022.14\"},{\"title\":\"Incremental Library Track\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2020/track_incremental.html\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2017\",\"url\":\"https://baldur.iti.kit.edu/sat-competition-2017/index.php?cat=incremental\"},{\"title\":\"IGMaxHS – An Incremental MaxSAT Solver with Support for XOR Clauses Ole Lübke1\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2410.15897\"}]\n\nI found relevant research on incremental SAT solving with IPASIR-UP and constraint propagation from 2024. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Overview\n\nThe IPASIR-UP interface enables solving according to a model with states and transitions within CDCL solving. It allows users to add new constraints to the problem while the solver is solving the query (within the CDCL loop), and use cases of the IPASIR-UP interface heavily rely on the incremental reasoning features of the underlying SAT solver.\n\n## External Propagation Integration\n\nWhen the solver is not in the Solving state, users can connect an external propagator via the function connect_external_propagator, which may be disconnected outside of Solving via disconnect_external_propagator, with at most one external propagator connected to a solver at any time.\n\n## Certification and Proof Formats\n\nThe proof formats LIDRUP and the new version of IDRUP easily allow capturing not just solver reasoning steps but user interactions as well, including IPASIR-UP use cases, with the only additional requirement that input clauses are allowed to be added between the query and answer status lines, capturing all clauses added by the external propagator during solving.\n\n## Implementation in SAT Solvers\n\nThe IPASIR-UP interface was implemented in the CaDiCaL SAT solver and also added to three other top-tier incremental SAT solvers: MiniSat 2.2.0, Glucose 4.2.1, and CryptoMiniSat 5.11.21.\n\n## Practical Applications\n\nIPASIR-UP supports the inclusion of more advanced custom propagation routines, enabling users to implement custom propagation that standard SAT solvers will not propagate. Recent applications include integration with SMT solvers like cvc5 for incremental constraint reasoning.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b18b90bd-1ee1-490c-8ce6-0d6389fb6eae","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:23.378Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d472ec1d-3d6d-4fb7-8173-3cbe910ef6c5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
