{"parentUuid":"58ee3787-5466-4fd5-bdf4-cd0a55f7142e","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab26579806bc582bd","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019a6mLQttP2ehmMgXsv1hxN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017USX7HKQLP43L5qhyHoR4J","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"reinforcement learning online bin packing 2024 2025 placement neural"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1354,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3933,"cache_read_input_tokens":20865,"output_tokens":294,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3933},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1354,"output_tokens":294,"cache_read_input_tokens":20865,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3933,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3933,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caox8hi1nv5YFYbxr9CqT","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"bbac7373-3c78-41ad-aab0-4484ccebfa8a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:28.164Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"4d811a52-2d7a-4d7b-9b10-5a7ae3563153","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"ab26579806bc582bd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TnfzX4oEtxcy9S3QXidjTh","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"online algorithms with predictions \"learning-augmented\" placement packing 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"[2406.03574] A Simple Learning-Augmented Algorithm for Online Packing with Concave Objectives\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.03574\"},{\"title\":\"Workshop on Learning-Augmented Algorithms\",\"url\":\"https://samsonzhou.github.io/ttic-2024-workshop-learning-augmented.html\"},{\"title\":\"[2411.08332] Learning-Augmented Algorithms for Online Concave Packing and Convex Covering Problems\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.08332\"},{\"title\":\"Learning-Augmented Algorithms for Online Concave Packing and Convex Covering Problems\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2411.08332v1\"},{\"title\":\"A Simple Learning-Augmented Algorithm for Online Packing with Concave Objectives\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2406.03574v1\"},{\"title\":\"A Simple Learning-Augmented Algorithm for Online ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2406.03574\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Learning-Augmented Algorithms for Online Concave Packing and Convex Covering Problems\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/385785861_Learning-Augmented_Algorithms_for_Online_Concave_Packing_and_Convex_Covering_Problems\"},{\"title\":\"Learning-Augmented Competitive Algorithms for Spatiotemporal Online Allocation with Deadline Constraints | Abstracts of the 2025 ACM SIGMETRICS International Conference on Measurement and Modeling of Computer Systems\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3726854.3727292\"},{\"title\":\"Algorithms with predictions\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/361673281_Algorithms_with_predictions\"},{\"title\":\"Learning-Augmented Algorithms for Online Linear and Semideﬁnite Programming\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2209.10614\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for your query on \"online algorithms with predictions learning-augmented placement packing 2024 2025\". Here are the key results:\n\n## Recent Research Highlights\n\nLearning-augmented algorithms have been extensively studied recently in the computer-science community, as predictions are especially useful for online algorithms making irrevocable decisions without knowledge of the future.\n\n### Key Papers from 2024-2025\n\n1. **Concave Packing Problems (June 2024)**: A paper titled \"A Simple Learning-Augmented Algorithm for Online Packing with Concave Objectives\" presents a framework using a switching strategy between advice and state-of-the-art online algorithms.\n\n2. **Concave Packing and Convex Covering (November 2024)**: \"Learning-Augmented Algorithms for Online Concave Packing and Convex Covering Problems\" was published on November 13, 2024. For online packing with concave objectives, the paper presents a strategy that switches between the advice and the state-of-the-art online algorithm.\n\n3. **Spatiotemporal Online Allocation (2025)**: ST-CLIP is a learning-augmented algorithm that takes advantage of predictions and achieves an optimal consistency-robustness trade-off, with evaluation in carbon-aware spatiotemporal workload management.\n\n### Core Concepts\n\nLearning-augmented algorithms aim to overcome the limitations of classical online algorithms when predictions are accurate, and still perform comparably when predictions are inaccurate. These algorithms maintain rigorous guarantees and high performance both when advice is accurate (consistency) and when advice is arbitrarily inaccurate (robustness).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6324b32c-2bcd-4454-bd22-bc4b97e77333","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:35.305Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4d811a52-2d7a-4d7b-9b10-5a7ae3563153","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e3d42bdc-07d9-47b2-816c-9ea870c4dec2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"ab26579806bc582bd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B6KP78ur2YvdbnSiMfndPN","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"online optimization framework Apache Beam Flink streaming combinatorial\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Apache Beam vs Flink: The Definitive Guide to Stream Processing\",\"url\":\"https://www.wallarm.com/cloud-native-products-101/apache-beam-vs-flink-stream-processing\"},{\"title\":\"Build a scalable, self-managed streaming infrastructure with Beam and Flink\",\"url\":\"https://beam.apache.org/blog/apache-beam-flink-and-kubernetes/\"},{\"title\":\"Apache Flink Runner\",\"url\":\"https://beam.apache.org/documentation/runners/flink/\"},{\"title\":\"Apache Beam: Introduction to Batch and Stream Data Processing\",\"url\":\"https://www.confluent.io/learn/apache-beam/\"},{\"title\":\"Build a scalable, self-managed streaming infrastructure with Beam and Flink: Tackling Autoscaling Challenges - Part 2\",\"url\":\"https://beam.apache.org/blog/apache-beam-flink-and-kubernetes-part2/\"},{\"title\":\"Apache Beam: How Beam Runs on Top of Flink | Apache Flink\",\"url\":\"https://flink.apache.org/2020/02/22/apache-beam-how-beam-runs-on-top-of-flink/\"},{\"title\":\"Behind the Scenes: Crafting an Autoscaler for Apache Beam in a High-Volume Streaming Environment\",\"url\":\"https://beam.apache.org/blog/apache-beam-flink-and-kubernetes-part3/\"},{\"title\":\"Apache Beam vs Flink 2026: Which Data Framework to Choose?\",\"url\":\"https://www.wildnetedge.com/blogs/apache-beam-vs-flink-which-data-processing-framework-wins\"},{\"title\":\"Apache Flink® — Stateful Computations over Data Streams | Apache Flink\",\"url\":\"https://flink.apache.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Apache Beam vs Apache Flink: Which One Suits You Best? | RisingWave\",\"url\":\"https://risingwave.com/blog/apache-beam-vs-apache-flink-which-one-suits-you-best/\"}]\n\nI've performed the web search for your query on online optimization framework Apache Beam Flink streaming combinatorial. Here's what the search results reveal:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**Framework Overview:**\nApache Flink and Apache Beam are open-source frameworks for parallel, distributed data processing at scale. Unlike Flink, Beam does not come with a full-blown execution engine of its own but plugs into other execution engines, such as Apache Flink, Apache Spark, or Google Cloud Dataflow.\n\n**Apache Beam:**\nApache Beam is an open-source, unified model for defining batch and streaming data-parallel processing pipelines. It is unified in the sense that you use a single API, in contrast to using a separate API for batch and streaming like it is the case in Flink.\n\n**Apache Flink:**\nApache Flink is a framework and distributed processing engine for stateful computations over unbounded and bounded data streams. Flink has been designed to run in all common cluster environments, perform computations at in-memory speed and at any scale.\n\n**Performance Comparison:**\nFlink generally outshines Beam in real-time scenarios, where low latency and the ability to handle stateful stream processing is critical. Beam tends to excel in batch processing environments due to its flexible runner architecture.\n\nThe search results primarily focus on comparisons between Apache Beam and Flink for streaming and batch processing, but don't specifically address \"combinatorial\" optimization frameworks. If you need more specific information about combinatorial optimization techniques or other aspects of these frameworks, please let me know.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"bcaf9cd0-82db-47e7-87cc-2ec3eaeb1a4c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:35.636Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e3d42bdc-07d9-47b2-816c-9ea870c4dec2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"58ee3787-5466-4fd5-bdf4-cd0a55f7142e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"ab26579806bc582bd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KbuTLpdnjsJ6nmcbGPednS","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"streaming algorithm 2D rectangle packing online geometric placement\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A Simple Solution for Shape Packing in 2D\",\"url\":\"https://www.gorillasun.de/blog/a-simple-solution-for-shape-packing-in-2d/\"},{\"title\":\"Online calculator: 2D Bin Packing Problem Solver\",\"url\":\"https://planetcalc.com/8634/\"},{\"title\":\"Exploring rectangle packing algorithms - David Colson\",\"url\":\"https://www.david-colson.com/2020/03/10/exploring-rect-packing.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - secnot/rectpack: Python 2D rectangle packing library · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/secnot/rectpack\"},{\"title\":\"Simple rectangle packing / Volodymyr Agafonkin | Observable\",\"url\":\"https://observablehq.com/@mourner/simple-rectangle-packing\"},{\"title\":\"Strip packing problem - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strip_packing_problem\"},{\"title\":\"Frontiers | Two-dimensional irregular packing problems: A review\",\"url\":\"https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/mechanical-engineering/articles/10.3389/fmech.2022.966691/full\"},{\"title\":\"Transformer-based placement heuristic for online 2D strip packing problem - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0360835225006102\"},{\"title\":\"Optimal Rectangle Packing: An Absolute Placement ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1402.0557\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient Algorithms for 2-D Rectangle packing\",\"url\":\"https://cgi.csc.liv.ac.uk/~epa/\"}]\n\nI've completed a web search for your query. Here are the key findings about streaming algorithms for 2D rectangle packing and online geometric placement:\n\n## Overview of the Problem\n\nThe strip packing problem is a 2-dimensional geometric minimization problem where given a set of axis-aligned rectangles and a strip of bounded width and infinite height, the goal is to determine an overlapping-free packing of the rectangles into the strip, minimizing its height.\n\n## Online vs. Offline Approaches\n\nWhile most approaches consider offline problems where the entire set of rectangles to be packed is known in advance, in many practical situations with time or space constraints, the items are provided sequentially, or the order of packing is predetermined, leading to online 2D-SPP problems where packing decisions are made consecutively and immediately.\n\n## Key Algorithms\n\nOne implementation of 2D bin packing problem solving relies on Maximal Rectangles Algorithms, which is an extension of the Guillotine Split heuristic and shows excellent results for offline packing, with the idea being to keep track of all maximal free rectangular spaces available after placing an object into the container.\n\nA skyline-based algorithm loops through open nodes along the \"skyline\" trying to fit a rectangle spanning one or more of them, and when it finds a place to put its rectangle, it needs to find all the nodes underneath that new skyline level made by the rectangle, and remove, or shrink them.\n\nA simple shelf technique is used by ordering the rectangles according to a sorting rule like decreasing width, increasing height, etc., and then greedily packing them one by one in this order over package shelves according to some rule, like Bottom-Left, Next-Fit, First-Fit.\n\n## Complexity\n\nThe rectangle packing problem is what's called an NP-hard (non-deterministic polynomial) problem, and consequently, there are countless different algorithms that \"solve\" the problem to some degree, but all have tradeoffs and issues.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"a695b5cf-3786-4f24-9eb8-e92bf94fa0b9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:36.052Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"58ee3787-5466-4fd5-bdf4-cd0a55f7142e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"bbac7373-3c78-41ad-aab0-4484ccebfa8a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"ab26579806bc582bd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017USX7HKQLP43L5qhyHoR4J","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"reinforcement learning online bin packing 2024 2025 placement neural\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"[2403.12420] Bin Packing Optimization via Deep Reinforcement Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.12420\"},{\"title\":\"GOPT: Generalizable Online 3D Bin Packing via Transformer-based Deep Reinforcement Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2409.05344v2\"},{\"title\":\"One4Many-StablePacker: An Efficient Deep Reinforcement Learning Framework for the 3D Bin Packing Problem\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.10057v1\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Xiong5Heng/GOPT: [IEEE RA-L 2024] GOPT: Generalizable Online 3D Bin Packing via Transformer-based Deep Reinforcement Learning · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Xiong5Heng/GOPT\"},{\"title\":\"One4Many-StablePacker: An Efficient Deep Reinforcement Learning Framework\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2510.10057\"},{\"title\":\"An Efficient Deep Reinforcement Learning Model for Online 3D Bin Packing Combining Object Rearrangement and Stable Placement\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2408.09694v1\"},{\"title\":\"Deep Reinforcement Learning Method with Integrated Rotation and Placement Strategies for Solving the 2D Bin Packing Problem\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/397874286_Deep_Reinforcement_Learning_Method_with_Integrated_Rotation_and_Placement_Strategies_for_Solving_the_2D_Bin_Packing_Problem\"},{\"title\":\"[2408.09694] An Efficient Deep Reinforcement Learning Model for Online 3D Bin Packing Combining Object Rearrangement and Stable Placement\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.09694\"},{\"title\":\"Learning practically feasible policies for online 3D bin packing | Science China Information Sciences | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11432-021-3348-6\"},{\"title\":\"Online 3D Bin Packing with Fast Stability Validation and Stable Rearrangement Planning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2507.09123v1\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here are recent developments in reinforcement learning applied to online bin packing with neural networks and placement strategies:\n\n## Recent Key Papers (2024-2025)\n\n**GOPT (2024):** GOPT is a generalizable online 3D Bin Packing approach via Transformer-based deep reinforcement learning (DRL). The method includes a Placement Generator module to yield finite subspaces as placement candidates and the representation of the bin, along with a Packing Transformer that fuses the features of the items and bin.\n\n**One4Many-StablePacker (October 2025):** The One4Many-StablePacker (O4M-SP) framework addresses limitations by enabling the model's ability to generalize across bins with varied dimensions, particularly those not encountered during training, without requiring retraining. The framework emphasizes the model's explicit integration of stability-related constraints to ensure real-world feasibility.\n\n**Deep Reinforcement Learning with Placement Strategy (August 2024):** This presents an efficient deep reinforcement learning (DRL) framework for online 3D bin packing (3D-BPP), addressing real-world physical constraints.\n\n**Online 3D Bin Packing with Stability Validation (July 2025):** A framework integrates packing policy with structural stability validation and heuristic planning, introducing the Load Bearable Convex Polygon (LBCP) concept for computationally efficient stable loading positions, and a Stable Rearrangement Planning (SRP) module that rearranges existing items while maintaining stability.\n\n## Common Approaches\n\nRecent methods use modified Pointer Networks with encoder-decoder-attention modules for optimal packing order, combined with placement strategies based on height maps to arrange objects while preventing collisions.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ae5f1206-0603-48ec-87eb-0b4a1eec365f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:36.196Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bbac7373-3c78-41ad-aab0-4484ccebfa8a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
