{"parentUuid":"69b2c5cf-11b0-421e-ab78-bdabd7a24984","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab26579806bc582bd","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_016pENKanThBPEE2SpjGiRUH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FQhEWd1v7LuLeF1fCsfTyd","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"online algorithm\" \"exact\" optimal feasible incompatible competitive ratio"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7124,"cache_read_input_tokens":24798,"output_tokens":229,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7124},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":229,"cache_read_input_tokens":24798,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7124,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7124,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caox9esPMekEA1LvmFZNP","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"ca1ec311-f321-4e4d-bfda-7df1be86a146","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:46.705Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"2e5aa909-da04-4706-bded-c56f5a2656ed","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"ab26579806bc582bd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Uvdc9wYNtNWZUV1Ks1RyWv","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT incremental solving warm start hint reuse previous solution\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Coding Patterns - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/06_coding_patterns.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy Release 0.9.24 Tias Guns Oct 06, 2025\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/_/downloads/en/latest/pdf/\"},{\"title\":\"Incremental solving using CP-SAT solver · Issue #2014 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/2014\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT, UNKNOWN status with complete solution hint · Issue #3750 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3750\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT and incremental usage under assumptions: possible?\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/n8u8yoF4UOI\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"On Incremental Core-Guided MaxSAT Solving\",\"url\":\"https://www.cis.upenn.edu/~mhnaik/papers/cp16.pdf\"}]\n\nI found relevant information about CP-SAT incremental solving, warm starting, and solution hints. Here's what the search results reveal:\n\n## Warm Starting and Solution Hints\n\nCP-SAT supports warm-starting, where the solver uses the previous solution as a starting point or \"hint\" for the next iteration. This technique can significantly speed up the solving process, as the solver can often use the previous solution as a good starting point for repair.\n\n## Repairing Infeasible Hints\n\nBecause repairing an infeasible hint can be computationally expensive, CP-SAT handles this process carefully. You can instruct CP-SAT to attempt repairing the hint by setting solver.parameters.repair_hint = True. Additionally, you can adjust the limit on how much effort CP-SAT should spend repairing the hint using solver.parameters.hint_conflict_limit—for example, setting solver.parameters.hint_conflict_limit = 10 controls how many conflicts CP-SAT will resolve before giving up.\n\n## Iterative Refinement Pattern\n\nAlthough reusing the solver class primarily spares you from rebuilding the model, each call to solve still initiates a new search from scratch. However, iteratively refining the model within the same solver instance is more intuitive to code than treating each iteration as an entirely new problem, and this pattern allows you to improve performance by leveraging features like warm-starting.\n\n## Practical Application\n\nFor daily replanning where yesterday's solution is available, use it as a hint. The solver doesn't blindly trust hints but uses them to focus initial search on promising regions.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"bc9d62f6-2d5d-4f40-9171-92c640c0b8a7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:52.911Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2e5aa909-da04-4706-bded-c56f5a2656ed","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ca1ec311-f321-4e4d-bfda-7df1be86a146","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"ab26579806bc582bd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FQhEWd1v7LuLeF1fCsfTyd","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"online algorithm\" \"exact\" optimal feasible incompatible competitive ratio\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Competitive analysis (online algorithm) - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Competitive_analysis_(online_algorithm)\"},{\"title\":\"Asymptotically Optimal Competitive Ratio for Online Allocation of Reusable Resources | Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/opre.2021.0695\"},{\"title\":\"Lecture 22 Online Algorithms\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~avrim/451f13/lectures/lect1107.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Online Algorithms Allan Borodin Denis Pankratov DRAFT: March 14, 2019\",\"url\":\"http://www.cs.toronto.edu/~bor/2420s19/papers/draft-ch1-8.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Asymptotically Optimal Competitive Ratio for Online ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2002.02430\"},{\"title\":\"Lecture 17 1 Online Algorithms and Competitive Analysis\",\"url\":\"https://theory.stanford.edu/~trevisan/cs261/lecture17.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"[2002.02430] Asymptotically Optimal Competitive Ratio for Online Allocation of Reusable Resources\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2002.02430\"},{\"title\":\"Online Algorithms Allan Borodin Denis Pankratov DRAFT: January 26, 2019\",\"url\":\"http://www.cs.toronto.edu/~bor/2420s19/our-online-text/chapters1-3.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Unified Algorithms for Online Learning and Competitive Analysis\",\"url\":\"https://proceedings.mlr.press/v23/buchbinder12/buchbinder12.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Optimal Competitive Online Algorithm\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/optimal-competitive-online-algorithm\"}]\n\nI've completed a web search for your query. Here are the key results:\n\n## Overview of Online Algorithms and Competitive Ratio\n\nCompetitive analysis is a method invented for analyzing online algorithms, in which the performance of an online algorithm (which must satisfy an unpredictable sequence of requests, completing each request without being able to see the future) is compared to the performance of an optimal offline algorithm that can view the sequence of requests in advance.\n\nAn algorithm is competitive if its competitive ratio—the ratio between its performance and the offline algorithm's performance—is bounded.\n\n## Optimal Competitive Ratios\n\nAn optimal competitive online algorithm is an online algorithm that achieves the smallest possible competitive ratio—i.e., the strongest worst-case performance guarantee relative to the offline optimum—for a given online optimization problem. The competitive ratio is defined as the supremum, over all possible inputs, of the ratio between the cost (or profit) of the algorithm and that of the optimal offline solution with complete future information.\n\n## Feasibility and Analysis Methods\n\nA novel approach has been developed by creating a certificate of optimality that is LP free, i.e., not based on LP duality. This involves proposing a system of linear inequalities such that proving feasibility of the system certifies competitiveness of the online algorithm being analyzed.\n\nThe search results provide comprehensive information on competitive analysis, optimal competitive ratios, and the mathematical frameworks used to analyze online algorithms, particularly addressing feasibility and performance guarantees.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"a6d4958e-1c2a-493a-b75a-cf678b022e6a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:53.469Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ca1ec311-f321-4e4d-bfda-7df1be86a146","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"69b2c5cf-11b0-421e-ab78-bdabd7a24984","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"39d21099-a8f4-47b7-adde-933641c1bb9e","agentId":"ab26579806bc582bd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UWATaPnRYRJEfutZP9SmJB","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Benders decomposition incremental cuts streaming candidates anytime master problem\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Benders decomposition - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benders_decomposition\"},{\"title\":\"OR in an OB World: Benders Decomposition Then and Now\",\"url\":\"https://orinanobworld.blogspot.com/2011/10/benders-decomposition-then-and-now.html\"},{\"title\":\"Speeding Up Logic-Based Benders Decomposition by Strengthening Cuts with Graph Neural Networks | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-53969-5_3\"},{\"title\":\"Benders Decomposition — AIMMS User's Guide\",\"url\":\"https://documentation.aimms.com/user-guide/aimms-ide/CPLEX/CPLEX_Benders_Decomposition.html\"},{\"title\":\"Benders decomposition - JuMP-dev\",\"url\":\"https://jump.dev/JuMP.jl/stable/tutorials/algorithms/benders_decomposition/\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Accelerating Benders decomposition with heuristic master problem solutions\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/262470973_Accelerating_Benders_decomposition_with_heuristic_master_problem_solutions\"},{\"title\":\"Implementing the branch-and-cut approach for a general purpose Benders’ decomposition framework - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0377221720307505\"},{\"title\":\"Implementing Automatic Benders Decomposition in a Modern MIP Solver\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/7506.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"OR in an OB World: Benders Decomposition with Integer Subproblems\",\"url\":\"https://orinanobworld.blogspot.com/2013/07/benders-decomposition-with-integer.html\"},{\"title\":\"Logic-Based Benders Decomposition - John Hooker\",\"url\":\"https://johnhooker.tepper.cmu.edu/encyLBBD.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about the concepts in your query related to Benders decomposition:\n\n## Core Benders Decomposition Framework\n\nBenders decomposition relies on an iterative procedure that chooses successive values without considering the inner problem except through a set of cut constraints that are created through a pass-back mechanism. The variables of the original problem are divided into two subsets so that a first-stage master problem is solved over the first set of variables, and the values for the second set of variables are determined in a second-stage subproblem.\n\n## Incremental Cuts\n\nTo speed up results you might want to do an incremental Benders decomposition, adding Benders cuts derived from any solution found in the master problem instead of waiting till optimality proof; which basically means embedding in an incumbent callback. This approach contrasts with traditional methods where you solve the master problem till optimality, compute the \"deepest\" benders cuts with a MIP, and then solve from scratch a new master with benders cuts.\n\n## Streaming Candidates and Anytime Solutions\n\nSome implementations use option 0 (wait for a new candidate incumbent before adding cuts) while others use option 1 (aggressively seek cuts at every node, perhaps by rounding the node solution or passing a fractional master solution to the subproblem). Before letting a solution be accepted, you have to check that it is a solution of the whole problem and possibly correct its objective value.\n\n## Cut Generation in Master Problem\n\nBD effectively handles the explosion in the number of constraints describing the problem by employing a delayed constraint generation algorithm. You pass a candidate incumbent solution, solve the subproblem and either bless the incumbent, return an optimality cut if the subproblem is feasible but the master problem solution incorrectly estimates the objective contribution, or return a feasibility cut if the subproblem is infeasible.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c18c3777-3dc6-4206-b4a7-4b6dba0dd406","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:55.448Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"69b2c5cf-11b0-421e-ab78-bdabd7a24984","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c18c3777-3dc6-4206-b4a7-4b6dba0dd406","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ab26579806bc582bd","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01EwZtuNNtFiN69ySBgXJHtX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough material. Let me now produce the focused report.\n\n---\n\n# 调研报告：streaming / online / incremental optimization 在 placement / packing 上的应用\n\n## 1. 概念辨析（关键，先把术语对齐）\n\n学术界\"online\"在 placement/packing 里有**两个完全不同的含义**，调研时要分开看：\n\n- **Online algorithm（理论意义）**：物品**按到达顺序不可逆地放置**，决策一旦做出不能撤销，跟离线最优比 competitive ratio。本质上 **sub-optimal**。\n- **Anytime / incremental（工程意义）**：求解器内部**持续优化**，可中途取当前最佳解，输入仍可以是 batch。本质上**仍可达到最优**，只是给出\"任何时刻可终止\"的工程性质。\n\n**这两者必须拆开判断对我们的价值**——前者跟我们 certified_exact 直接冲突，后者高度相关。\n\n## 2. 关键论文 / 框架\n\n**Online bin packing（理论）**：\n- AH 算法把 asymptotic competitive ratio 压到 1.5783（首次破 1.58 壁垒），下界 1.54278。\n- Online 3D BPP 的 SOTA 是 GOPT（Transformer-based RL，IEEE RA-L 2024）和 One4Many-StablePacker（2025）。\n- **共同特点：解都是近似的，没有最优证书**。\n\n**Learning-augmented online algorithms（2024–2025 热点）**：\n- 给 online 算法配\"prediction\"，预测准时接近最优（consistency），预测错时退回 worst-case 保底（robustness）。\n- 代表论文：Im 等 *A Simple Learning-Augmented Algorithm for Online Packing with Concave Objectives*（arXiv 2406.03574，2024.6）；*Learning-Augmented Algorithms for Online Concave Packing and Convex Covering*（arXiv 2411.08332，2024.11）。\n- 对我们而言：**这是 RL 排序 hint 的理论基础**，跟 S4 AI dataset 路线天然对齐。\n\n**Incremental SAT / IPASIR-UP（2024）**：\n- IPASIR-UP 把外部 propagator 接入 CDCL 主循环，可在 solving 过程中动态加约束。已经实装到 CaDiCaL、MiniSat、Glucose、CryptoMiniSat。\n- 对应证书格式 LIDRUP/IDRUP 能记录 user 交互步骤——也就是说**增量求解仍能产生形式化证明**。\n- 对 **CP-SAT 的影响：有限**。OR-Tools 维护者多次表态（GitHub issue #2014）CP-SAT 不支持真正的增量，每次 `Solve()` 是从头搜的。能利用的只有 **solution hint + warm start + repair_hint = True**。\n\n**Anytime CP-SAT**：\n- 通过 `CpSolverSolutionCallback.on_solution_callback` 拿到每个改进解。\n- 实操上\"anytime\"已经存在——你在 168h 的任何时刻 kill 都能拿到当前 incumbent。\n\n**Benders 增量 cut**：\n- 经典做法：incumbent callback 里 lazy 地加 Benders cut，不等 master 求到最优就开始切。我们当前已经是 LBBD（Logic-Based Benders Decomposition），**但 master 是每个候选独立重建一遍**。这是真正可优化的点。\n\n**Streaming framework（Beam/Flink）**：\n- **明确排除**。这些是数据处理框架，不是组合优化框架。我们想要的\"frontier 当 stream\"是消息队列模式，用 Python 自己的 `multiprocessing.Queue` 或 Redis Stream 就够了，没必要上 Beam/Flink，工程开销不成比例。\n\n## 3. online vs batch 在 placement 上的对比\n\n| 维度 | Batch（当前） | Online（理论） | Anytime/Incremental（工程） |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 最优性 | 可证最优 | sub-optimal（ratio < 1） | 可证最优（中途解非最优但终态最优）|\n| 决策可逆 | 是 | **否** | 是 |\n| 候选到达 | 一次给齐 | 逐个到达 | 一次给齐，但内部边算边出 |\n| 跟 certified_exact | 兼容 | **冲突** | 兼容 |\n| 工程改造量 | — | 推倒重来 | 中等（hint 复用、Benders 持久化）|\n\n## 4. 对我们项目的可行性判断\n\n**直接采用 online algorithm（理论意义）：排除。**\n理由：online 算法的 1.5783 competitive ratio 意味着面积可能差到最优的 63%，这跟 PROJECT_LOCK 里 `max_lex(area, min_side)` 的 certified_exact 语义直接冲突。AI safety contract 也明确禁止 AI 路径产出 proof。\n\n**采用 anytime + incremental 工程范式：强烈建议，且很多已经在做。**\n\n具体可行的迁移点（按工程量从低到高）：\n\n1. **CP-SAT solution hint 跨候选复用（低）**：当前每个 outer 候选独立 solve，相邻候选的 master 解高度相似。把上一候选的 master 解作为 hint 传给下一个，配 `repair_hint=True`、`hint_conflict_limit=10`。S6 worker tuning 里可以加这一项。\n\n2. **Frontier 当 stream + worker pool 持续 pop（中）**：把 outer search 的 frontier 改成 `multiprocessing.Queue`，scheduler 持续 push 新候选，worker 持续 pop。crash resilience 已经做完（commit 45aa0e8），改造成本不高。这跟 ε-Certified 路线**天然加成**——anytime 性质让你在 168h 任何点 kill 都拿到一个带 ε bound 的解。\n\n3. **Benders cut 跨候选持久化（中高）**：当前每个候选 LBBD 从空 cut pool 开始，但很多 binding/routing infeasibility cut 在不同候选间是**结构性可复用的**（同一基地、同一 facility）。把 cut pool 序列化成 campaign-level artifact，新候选启动时载入相关 cut。需要谨慎设计 cut 的\"上下文 key\"（候选指纹的哪些维度决定 cut 是否适用），否则会污染证明。建议先做 shadow 实验。\n\n4. **Learning-augmented 候选排序（已规划）**：S4 AI dataset 路线就是干这个，2024 的 learning-augmented packing 论文是其理论支撑。order_only，不动 proof。\n\n**不建议的方向：**\n- **IPASIR-UP / 真增量 SAT**：CP-SAT 不支持，要切到 CaDiCaL 这类原生 SAT 路线，等于推倒重来 80% 的代码，ROI 极低。\n- **RL 直接出 placement**：违反 AI safety contract（不能替代 proof source）。只能做 hint。\n- **Apache Beam/Flink**：杀鸡用牛刀，本机 4 process pool 已经够用。\n\n## 5. 一句话结论\n\n**online 理论排除，anytime/incremental 工程吸收**。优先级：CP-SAT hint 复用 > frontier streaming > Benders cut 持久化 > learning-augmented ordering（已在 S4）。预估三项加起来对 168h campaign 的吞吐提升在 1.3–2x 区间，不动 certified_exact 语义。\n\n## Sources\n\n- [A Simple Learning-Augmented Algorithm for Online Packing with Concave Objectives (arXiv 2406.03574)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.03574)\n- [Learning-Augmented Algorithms for Online Concave Packing and Convex Covering Problems (arXiv 2411.08332)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.08332)\n- [A new and improved algorithm for online bin packing (Balogh et al., AH algorithm)](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1707.01728)\n- [A new lower bound for classic online bin packing (arXiv 1807.05554)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1807.05554)\n- [GOPT: Generalizable Online 3D Bin Packing via Transformer-based DRL (IEEE RA-L 2024)](https://arxiv.org/html/2409.05344v2)\n- [One4Many-StablePacker: Efficient DRL Framework for 3D BPP (arXiv 2510.10057)](https://arxiv.org/html/2510.10057v1)\n- [Certifying Incremental SAT Solving (Fazekas et al., LPAR 2024)](https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/FazekasPollittFleuryBiere-LPAR24.pdf)\n- [IPASIR-UP / IDRUP proof format (JAIR 2024)](https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/download/16163/27111/42883)\n- [CP-SAT Primer — Coding Patterns (warm start, repair_hint)](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/06_coding_patterns.html)\n- [OR-Tools issue #2014: Incremental solving using CP-SAT](https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/2014)\n- [Logic-Based Benders Decomposition (John Hooker)](https://johnhooker.tepper.cmu.edu/encyLBBD.pdf)\n- [Speeding Up LBBD with Graph Neural Networks (CPAIOR 2024)](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-53969-5_3)\n- [Transformer-based placement heuristic for online 2D strip packing problem](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0360835225006102)\n- [Competitive Analysis (Wikipedia)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Competitive_analysis_(online_algorithm))"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1295,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2989,"cache_read_input_tokens":31922,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2989,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoxB52UVVL593GHd4uT1","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"d28c2376-877d-4ced-bef2-17f8371269de","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:55:00.203Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
